  "title": "Ana Maria NDE 4937",
  "date": "Febrero 1981",
  "content": "In the winter of 1981, I was on the way to the beach with a friend, and we were going down the steps (around 10:30 in the morning), when suddenly, as my friend tells it, I fainted. Though I felt nothing, I just remember rising up. There was a brilliant sun, giving me a special, soft, warmth, which did not burn me. I could hear beautiful music and I could see birds flying beside me, it was an incredible peace, something extraordinary; I had never felt this before, it was a beautiful feeling, and I didn't want to come back. My friend says I fell to the ground and became cold (we were on the resting-stage of the descent), and some people surrounded me and tried to resuscitate me. I was as if dead, and my friend was shouting to me, talking, and crying, for about three minutes, and she shouted so much that I woke up as if nothing had happened. I felt nothing (bad), on the contrary, I was still trying to hear the lovely music, which was gone, nor could I see birds flying. I was in mild shock, and went to the clinic where the doctor said that my breakfast had not agreed with me that day, nothing more.",
